<task id="001" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Spike MCP server, echo tool and test widget</title>
    <phase>0 Platform spike</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies code files (.cs, .ts) on the spike branch, and the spike is deployed to the dev BFF behind live auth</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Single throwaway spike with explicit references (design.md §13, knowledge/mcp-apps samples); no production code merges</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Runs in its own worktree on spike/spaarkeai-mcp-phase0, so it shares no files with 011 or 017</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, minimal-api, typescript, frontend, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Cut spike/spaarkeai-mcp-phase0 from origin/master in its own worktree and build the smallest stateless MCP server in the BFF that Phase 0 needs: /mcp/legal-operations with an echo tool and an OBO WhoAmI tool, a second route with a different tool set (T13), and a single-file test widget at 1, 3 and 6 MB, so T0, T5, T13 and the size/init tests can run on the dev BFF.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, the ModelContextProtocol C# SDK and MCP Apps widgets.</role>
  <goal>The spike branch exists (never merged) with a stateless, authenticated MCP endpoint, two tool sets on two routes, a spike_whoami OBO tool and a test widget resource in three sizes; local protocol checks pass; measurements are recorded in notes/spikes/phase0-spike-measurements.md on the project branch; the owner has a SHA to approve for the dev deploy.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-19 and design §13: Phase 0 gates the project (T5 gates everything, T0 gates the MCP build, T13 decides the route mechanism, Size decides NFR-03). Ontology condition 1 (project CLAUDE.md §3): no dev BFF deploy from work/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1 until ontology's #2580/#2579 pair deploys, so Phase 0 runs from a master-based spike branch, deployed only with the owner's per-SHA go in unified-access-control-r2's session.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/Spike/SpikeMcpEndpoints.cs (spike branch only)</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spike-test/ (spike branch only: Vite single-file test widget)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj (spike branch only: ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore 2.3.1)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs (spike branch only)</file>
      <file role="new">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/spikes/phase0-spike-measurements.md (project branch)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Workspace/WorkspaceMatterEndpoints.cs:196-200 (disable response buffering)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/DataverseUserClient.cs (OBO WhoAmI as the caller)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">knowledge/mcp-apps/trey-research/src/mcpserver/widgets/src/hooks/useMcpApp.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/CreateMatterWizard/vite.config.ts (vite-plugin-singlefile)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/design.md §13 (Phase 0 tests) and §11 (hosting)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">No prerequisite task; startable in Wave 1.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">All spike code lives only on spike/spaarkeai-mcp-phase0 in a separate worktree cut from origin/master; nothing from the spike is merged into work/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1 or master; only the measurements note is written on the project branch (ontology condition 1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every spike route calls .RequireAuthorization() on the default workforce scheme; the spike adds no anonymous route and changes no authentication scheme or AuthorizationModule.cs code (root CLAUDE.md §9).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">spike_whoami returns only the caller's systemuserid and the decoded aud, scp, tid and oid claim NAMES with a present/absent flag for each, never the token or claim values beyond those ids, and logs nothing but ids and timings.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-052">The spike adds no background work; it runs stateless (SDK default, no session store).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Deploys of the spike happen only with the owner's explicit go for that SHA in unified-access-control-r2's session (project CLAUDE.md §5); this task never deploys on its own.</constraint>
  </constraints>

